# W04 final ten-vitamin association disposition

**Document one common nominal ten-vitamin recipe association now, linked to both authentic Mc and generic CB Wolfe source profiles. Retain the existing source records separately; do not install either new source-number owner, select an exclusive owner, or merge maintained records.**

This is a completed bounded disposition, not another hold on whether the nominal recipe can be represented. The original McCas methods supply positive preparation evidence beyond matching numbers. Together with the complete JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 tables and the actual Mc/CB source blocks, they support a practical nominal convention under §3 while every source-specific detail remains visible. A common component list alone would not establish exact entity identity.

Use report-local group `TENVIT-NOMINAL-RECIPE-GROUP-001`, displayed as “Common nominal ten-vitamin recipe (source-qualified preparations).” It is reconciliation metadata, not an ingredient CURIE, new owner, exported node or identity predicate. Future bounded owner notes may describe the positive comparison and cite the exact sources. Do not use the comparison to add resolving synonyms, exact matches, transferred occurrences or direct component support for a more specific source profile.

