|---|---|
| Mc_vitamins | Existing identifier/path/history; ten literal G_PER_L solutes, D,L-calcium pantothenate, generic B12 and X100 metadata. No water or actual CB preparation inferred from the independent McCas protocol. |
| Generic CB Wolfe | Actual a019 W08 dependent origin, authentic beforeimage and W09/W08 event authors; ten MG_PER_L solutes, explicit cyanocobalamin, generic calcium UNMAPPED, nine bounded child references and X100 metadata. Whole-stock assertion remains UNKNOWN. |
| JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 | All ten masses plus 1 L added water; generic calcium/B12 UNMAPPED; COMPLETE only relative to the eleven printed inputs. Keep JCM197 N₂ stock filtration and each NBRC procedure source-local. No final-volume concentration or gas-state equivalence inferred. |

Mc’s separate SCI-TENVIT-003 correction can proceed without waiting for owner consolidation: preserve the D,L name and 0.005 G_PER_L, withdraw the unsupported D-specific child reference/use UNMAPPED unless an exact same-form child is verified, and qualify the crosswalk note. This review uses the current Mc beforeimage with that prospective narrow correction explicitly conditional; it accepts no unseen successor bytes.

The two immutable null-before source proposals, `C-P-JCM197` and `vm1201-prop-nbrc903-vitamin`, are **not selected for owner installation**. Preserve both payloads, authorship and every original case/proposal link as evidence for the nominal group. Do not rewrite them as existing-owner origins. The genuine W08 CB dependency remains a separate authentic existing-owner correction, with W10’s independent complete-payload review retained.

Exact finished-stock/entity equivalence and a unique JCM/NBRC→Mc or CB owner edge remain unestablished. Neither relation is needed to document this nominal association. If later authorized, a provenance-preserving consolidation can assess complete owners and source routes; the present evidence does not choose a winner by author or filename, and does not require lot assays to retain the recipe.

All eight original case objects, 71 CM occurrences, 84 separate KG holds and six excluded contexts remain. Sixty-five is only an upper bound; zero new exact owner routes are approved. Source-specific JCM887, dose/unit, form, role and export holds remain. Actual ATCC2672 protocol evidence does not override current MD-VS’s positive phosphate/product boundary. TV001–004 and the separate genuine NCMA phosphate claim remain. Stale nominal CB/phosphate wording remains existing #1237 follow-up.

